  "openQuestions": [
    "Counts are fetched with date = format(new Date(), 'yyyyMMdd') (the browser's today), not the encounter's 기준일시. For a back-dated chart the limit is checked against today's counts. Should the server use the encounter service date?",
    "The count endpoint returns 한방첩약시범사업승인횟수 (approved counts). It is unknown whether the current encounter's own prescription is already included in the count; with '> 8' semantics the 9th approved prescription trips the limit. Server must decide whether to count before or after including the encounter being saved.",
    "The pcmd-count query has no `enabled` guard, so it fires with doctorId undefined (URL .../doctor/undefined) before a doctor is chosen. Server-side the rule should require a doctor.",
    "Month/year windows (calendar month/year vs rolling) are defined only by the server endpoint; the client never computes them.",
    "Overflow handling in the UI: a watch on the counts sets 첩건본인부담률구분코드 = U whenever HLt is true, overriding a user choice; there is no server-side enforcement visible in the client."
  ]
